cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HyMED Python — Hydrologic Model Evaluation for Drought (Python translation)"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this Python translation and the
  original HyMED R package (Simeone and Foks, 2024) referenced below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ryan
    family-names: van der Heijden
    email: rvanderh@uvm.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ryan-vanderHeijden/HyMED_Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python translation of the HyMED R package (Simeone and Foks, 2024) for
  evaluating hydrologic model streamflow output during periods of drought. It
  computes Weibull drought percentiles (with variable Julian-day or fixed
  thresholds and the Consecutive Dry Period Method for zero-flow periods)
  and a suite of comparison metrics between modeled and observed streamflow
  drought, including Cohen's kappa, Spearman's rho, percent bias, SD ratio, and
  annual drought signature metrics. Outputs are validated against the original R
  implementation.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - streamflow
  - drought
  - model evaluation
license: MIT
